- Frontend Implementation
    - Implement a frontend for navigating the lore.
        - Timeline View
        - Search Functionality
        - Sorting Options
        - Favorites/Bookmarks
        - Family Trees
            - Immediate family members first
            - Include extended family members using the connections in the family tree.
            - Allow collapsing and expanding branches of the family tree.
        - Character Profiles
        - Lore Subject Pages
        - Map View
        - Interactive Timelines
        - Notifications for Updates
        - In world books
            - Implement a system for creating and managing in world books.
            - Allow players to access in world books they are granted access to.
            - Bookcase view for displaying accessible in world books.
- Admin Implementation
    - In World Book Management
        - Language Selection for in world books.
        - Implement a system to manage in world books languages.
            - Connected to in world languages.
            - implement a system that allows hovering over certain words (highlighting them) to show what they were translated from.
            e.g. hovering over fire would show the original word in the source language.
            - Publish Date for each in world book translation.
            - Which fantasy language a book is available in.
    - Locations
        - Implement a Location Pinning System
        - Add a map overlay system for displaying political boundaries and regions.
        - Implement a system for marking locations of interest on the map.
        - Allow players to filter locations based on categories or tags.
        - Implement a system for linking locations to lore subjects.
- Backend Systems
    - Implement the player character management system
        - Backstory Management
        - Tag selection
    - Add tags to all lore systems, and implement filtering by tags.
        - Tag system entry comma separated and searchable (WordPress style)
        - Tag filtering for lore subjects
        - Allow Players to generate a lore document based on which tags they have access to.
        - Make some tags as a "Must be granted" before being given to players.
    - Add hidden lore subjects and what tags they are locked behind
        - Tier hidden lore subjects behind specific number of tags
        - Specify which tags unlock hidden lore subjects
        - Rank tags by importance or relevance
        - Allow sorting hidden lore subjects by tag importance or relevance
        - Implement tags as must-have for accessing certain hidden lore subjects.
    - Implement a system to mark lore subjects as needs-updating.
        - When using a wiki link, it should mark the referenced lore subject as needing update.
        - When a piece of lore gets flagged for update, it should say why it needs updating.
        - Implement a system to notify players when lore they have access to is updated.
    - Implement a storyteller system so that storytellers can create and update lore.
        - Implement a system to notify storytellers when lore subjects they updated or created got approved or rejected.
        - Storytellers should be able to see awaiting approval lore subjects they have submitted.
        - Implement a system for storytellers to edit their submitted lore subjects before approval.
        - Implement a system for storytellers to withdraw their submitted lore subjects before approval.
        - Implement a system for storytellers to see the status of their submitted lore subjects.
        - Implement a system for storytellers to receive feedback on rejected lore subjects.
        - Implement a system for storytellers to receive notifications when their submitted lore subjects are approved.
    - Current Notifications System should be extended to handle:
        - Email notifications for all implemented notification types.
        - Mobile notifications for all implemented notification types.
